WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.647
- Have you ever met Matt, I
was gonna ask, first of all?

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:03.430
- No and I'm so grateful to both of you.

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.860
You've given me so much
joy over my lifetime, so,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.010
over my lifetime, I make it
sound a thousand years old,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.150
but I was so excited to come today

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.240
and be sandwiched by you.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.225
- Oh cool, that's actually
why I love the panel,

00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:17.320
'cause I feel like people don't generally,

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.830
everybody thinks everybody
knows each other,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.950
like you go to some kind of
celebrity barbecue weekly

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:21.890
or something, yeah.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.510
I don't know anyone.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.588
- I gotta take off.

00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:26.380
(laughing)

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.350
- I actually don't wanna be here.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.260
So wait, you and I are
actually gonna be taking

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.790
Joey Tribiani down in a
Friends game, are you ready?

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.100
- I know, well, we can be
nice to him now, though,

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.760
'cause, you know, then
we'll kick his ass later.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.490
- Okay.
- Oh, okay, okay,

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.323
I was like, "Wait,

00:00:39.323 --> 00:00:40.510
"we're not gonna be
nice about it, Bellamy,"

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.300
but then you got there,
okay, you got there.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.130
No, you loved Friends though, right?

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.952
- Oh yeah, how about you guys?

00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:47.791
(audience cheering)

00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:49.750
- It's such a good show,
yeah, such a good show.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.220
But today's show is a
love letter to New York

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.620
and you just moved there, right?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.123
- Yes, I love it so much,
it my heart's home, I do.

00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:00.564
(audience clapping)

00:01:00.564 --> 00:01:02.150
- So you didn't grow up
there, right, though?

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.400
- No, I grew up in North Carolina,

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.630
Asheville, North Carolina,
in the mountains.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.915
- [Kelly] Our family live in Asheville.

00:01:05.915 --> 00:01:06.748
- Oh no, are you serious?

00:01:06.748 --> 00:01:09.380
- We have family in Asheville
and really in Granite Falls,

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.130
yeah, yeah, yeah.
- I didn't know that,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.360
but to get this job, it was
always like a holy grail,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.290
you know, to get a job that
wonderful in New York city

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.540
and now I just sit, I have
a tiny, little balcony

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.190
and I, you know, overlooks an avenue

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.023
and I just look an happy cry.
- Wait, so your apartment

00:01:23.023 --> 00:01:25.950
doesn't look like Monica, or Joey's?

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.561
- My apartment looks like this table.

00:01:27.561 --> 00:01:29.340
(laughing)

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.350
And I stand here sometimes
and here sometimes

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.870
and here sometimes and I love it!

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.180
- Have you shopped for apartments?

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.610
Did you shop for 'em or did you find--

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.880
- I did it all on StreetEasy.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.287
Have you guys ever used that StreetEasy?

00:01:39.287 --> 00:01:41.610
'Cause I was here, so
I wasn't in New York.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.797
I had to ask my friends,

00:01:42.797 --> 00:01:45.410
"Will you go to this
open house on Wednesday?"

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.720
But yeah, I was like,
till my thumbs fell off,

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.290
that's how I found my little apartment

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.620
and then it was all Ikea and Amazon

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.467
and I built my bed and
my dresser and all of it.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.703
(audience cheering)

00:01:55.703 --> 00:01:57.740
- I love Ikea.
- I know, me too.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.573
- You know what though?

00:01:58.573 --> 00:02:00.770
I think, Ikea, you should never,

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.450
you can really tell who
your true friends are.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.570
I don't think you should
build furniture like that

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:05.508
with loved ones.

00:02:05.508 --> 00:02:06.341
(laughing)

00:02:06.341 --> 00:02:07.460
I feel like it ends poorly.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.280
- I mean, 'cause they always say, like,

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.217
it's that little cartoon that is like,

00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:12.460
"This is a two person job,"

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.720
which I feel is angry
at the single people,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.130
so I do not accept.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.010
- So, Matt, do you have a store place

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.189
that you're crazy about, like
Ikea or anything like that?

00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:24.053
- You know, when we were doing Friends,

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:27.110
if we went to work and
we had a photo shoot,

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.030
or doing press for the show,
it was really consuming,

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.917
so when that ended, I kind of said,

00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:34.980
"I need to go out and
reengage with the world,"

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.470
and I discovered this place called Target,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.500
anybody heard of that?

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.333
(audience clapping)

00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:43.097
- I love Target.
- That was like, "Oh my God."

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.960
You can get baloney and motor
oil and pillows and fridges.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.080
- And jeans, you can get everything

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.450
and here's the thing about Target though,

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.620
it's like Alice in
Wonderland, the rabbit hole,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.480
you just go down, because
I go in for a spatula

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.480
and I come out with 500 dollars
worth of crap I don't need.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.970
- Yeah, when we shopped at
Whole Foods, was whole paycheck,

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.790
like that's my whole
paycheck, like, Target

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.730
and there's always something cute, yeah.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.506
- I'm in Target anonymous now.

00:03:11.506 --> 00:03:12.561
(laughing)

00:03:12.561 --> 00:03:14.880
- [Bellamy] I'm working through
it, I'm working through it.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.310
- But, I have to talk to you about this

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.581
because I completely stormed
into your dressing room.

00:03:19.581 --> 00:03:20.420
(laughing)

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.750
'Cause you kept me up till
1:30 in the morning last night.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.410
I was so excited to see Prodigal Son

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.177
and then I heard you were
coming on today and I was like,

00:03:29.177 --> 00:03:31.210
"God, I've been dying to
watch this for so long."

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.890
I was like, "I'll just watch
one episode, just so I know."

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.120
Seven episodes later, I'm in my bed

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.087
and my husband is snoring and I'm like,

00:03:39.087 --> 00:03:40.210
"I just have to know if,"

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.128
and I don't wanna ruin it,
so I'm not gonna say it,

00:03:42.128 --> 00:03:44.270
I'm not gonna say it, but
I had to know something

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.030
and they kept teasing you
and I had to keep watching

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:47.890
and it's so good.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.830
It's the highest rated new show right now.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.807
- It is, we're so lucky, yes, yes.

00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:55.240
- It's so good!
- We love making it,

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.073
we love doing it.

00:03:56.073 --> 00:03:57.890
I dunno if you guys have
seen it yet, it's sort of,

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.960
it's a show that asks the question

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.531
what if Hannibal Lecter were your father?

00:04:01.531 --> 00:04:03.210
- Or husband.
- Or your husband,

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.530
Michael Sheen plays that
character, he's my husband

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:08.003
and he gets carted off to
Hannibal Lecter land in like, 98.

00:04:08.003 --> 00:04:10.820
- He might secretly be psycho.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.110
- He's a very good actor.
- I am like, "Whoa."

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.323
- Let's not anger him.

00:04:14.323 --> 00:04:16.420
(laughing)

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:20.440
And Tom Payne from Walking Dead
plays our son, all grown up

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.040
and now he's a profiler

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.560
trying to atone for
the sins of his father.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.860
Yeah and it's got the family setup,

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.140
so it has heart and humor,

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.753
but it's got enough horror
to keep you awake at night.

00:04:28.753 --> 00:04:30.860
- Yeah, but it has humor too,

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.130
even the serial killer
kinda humor is funny

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.197
and I'm laughing at it and I'm like,

00:04:34.197 --> 00:04:35.887
"That's not funny, that's horrible."

00:04:35.887 --> 00:04:38.010
- But they make it funny.
- They do.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.423
- You know, you gotta
laugh to get through.

00:04:39.423 --> 00:04:42.200
- I love it, I am very
excited for this show for you.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.090
I mean, you're just going
from one hit show to the next,

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.998
so there you go, universe, you're welcome.

00:04:45.998 --> 00:04:46.831
(laughing)

